    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe endpoint/exception/handler/schema/openapi scaffolding is idiomatic and matches the existing siblings (`InvalidTelephoneException` + handler + escalation YAML, pipeline wiring after the normalize steps, `ApplyOwner`/schema/DTO changes). One structural issue, though:\n\n**Duplicated single-source-of-truth table \u2014 `CITY_REGION` is copied verbatim from `Owner`.**\n\n`Owner.java:204-215` already owns the fixed city-to-region table as the single source of truth, exposed via `getLocality()`:\n\n```java\n/** Fixed city-to-region table used to derive {@link #getLocality()}. */\nprivate static final Map<String, String> CITY_REGION = Map.of(\n    \"Sydney\", \"NSW\", \"Melbourne\", \"VIC\", \"Brisbane\", \"QLD\");\n```\n\n`ValidateOwnerPostcode` re-declares an identical constant:\n\n```java\n/** Fixed city-to-region table, matching {@code Owner.getLocality()}. */\nprivate static final Map<String, String> CITY_REGION = Map.of(\n    \"Sydney\", \"NSW\", \"Melbourne\", \"VIC\", \"Brisbane\", \"QLD\");\n```\n\nThe Javadoc \u2014 \"matching `Owner.getLocality()`\" \u2014 is itself an admission that the two must be kept in sync by hand. There are now two definitions of the same domain fact; adding a city (or correcting a region) requires editing both, and they can silently diverge (e.g. postcode validation and the returned `locality` disagreeing for the same owner). A maintainer would not expect the region table to live in two unrelated units.\n\nSuggested fix: keep the table in one place and have the validator reuse it. Since the region\u2192city mapping is a domain concept already living on `Owner`, expose the lookup once (e.g. a `static String Owner.regionOf(String city)` that `getLocality()` also delegates to) and call that from `ValidateOwnerPostcode` instead of re-declaring `CITY_REGION`. The new `REGION_POSTCODES` map is genuinely postcode-validation-specific and is fine to keep in this class.\n\nEverything else (the exception being checked, the handler using the shared `ProblemDetails` helper, wiring into both POST and PUT with matching `govern`, the four schema files, and the openapi entry) is coherent and additive.",
